<h2 id="taxes-licensing">Brookhaven licensing and Georgia taxes</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>City business license:</strong> Brookhaven issues an Occupational Tax Certificate that expires each December 31. Home-based businesses also file a Home Occupation form governed by the zoning code.</li>
  <li><strong>State income tax:</strong> Georgia's flat rate is 5.19% for 2026.</li>
  <li><strong>Self-employment tax:</strong> 15.3% federal on net profit, on top of federal income tax. Estimate it with the <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Sales tax:</strong> selling physical products means registering with the Georgia Department of Revenue. Most personal services, like cleaning and pet sitting, aren't subject to sales tax.</li>
  <li><strong>Short-term rentals:</strong> rules for renting a home or room are set by the city's zoning code. Check with Brookhaven's Planning and Development department before listing.</li>
</ul>

